Approach 3 — BFS Level Order + Take Last Node

This is the most direct solution.

Since right-side view means:

rightmost node at every level

and BFS processes one level at a time, simply take:

if (i == size - 1)

for every level.

This is the approach used in your code.

Your Code
/**
 * Definition for a binary tree node.
 * public class TreeNode {
 *     int val;
 *     TreeNode left;
 *     TreeNode right;
 *     TreeNode() {}
 *     TreeNode(int val) { this.val = val; }
 *     TreeNode(int val, TreeNode left, TreeNode right) {
 *         this.val = val;
 *         this.left = left;
 *         this.right = right;
 *     }
 * }
 */
class Solution {
    public List<Integer> rightSideView(TreeNode root) {
        List<Integer> al=new ArrayList<>();
        if(root==null){
            return al;
        }

        Queue<TreeNode> q=new LinkedList<>();
        q.add(root);
        while(!q.isEmpty()){
            ArrayList<Integer> list=new ArrayList<>();
            int size=q.size();
            for(int i=0;i<size;i++){
                TreeNode curr=q.poll();
                if(i==size-1){
                    al.add(curr.val);
                }
                if(curr.left!=null){
                    q.add(curr.left);
                }
                if(curr.right!=null){
                    q.add(curr.right);
                }
            }
            al.addAll(list);
        }
        return al;
    }
}
